    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'll start with the timestamp cross-referencing. One thing though—the timing is what's bothering me. They don't seem to follow any weekly or monthly schedule; they just appear out of nowhere, randomly. It's like they're just... slipping through the cracks of the system. Is there a way to specifically look for 'ghost' entries or transactions that don't leave a clear paper trail in the procurement software?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To hunt for \"ghost\" entries, focus your analysis on the data entry or user access logs, looking for transactions created by generic accounts or outside standard operating hours. Specifically, filter for entries lacking a corresponding, valid associated purchase order number, even if the ledger entry itself is present. If possible, isolate transactions posted as manual journal entries rather than standard invoice/PO receipts, as these often bypass automated controls. This targeted review helps pinpoint entries that may have been manually inserted without proper upstream documentation.",
